From: x86.mov movfuscator-wasm
Subject: [PATCH] build.sh: build LCC as C89 under modern gcc

Two separate breakages, both from gcc moving its defaults forward.

gcc 14 promoted -Wimplicit-int and -Wimplicit-function-declaration
(and -Wint-conversion) from warnings to errors by default. LCC's
src/*.c and yacc-generated y.tab.c rely on these K&R-era constructs,
so the lcc make step fails before rcc/cpp can be built. Demote these
three back to warnings.

gcc 15 made C23 the default dialect, which reserves `constexpr`.
LCC declares `extern Tree constexpr(int);` in src/c.h, so every
translation unit including it now fails to parse:

    src/c.h:516:1: error: 'constexpr' used with 'extern'

`-std=gnu89` is the honest fix rather than renaming LCC's function:
this *is* a 1990s C89 codebase, the dialect it was written for is
exactly what it should be compiled as, and pinning it keeps the next
default-dialect bump from breaking the build again. It also subsumes
the three warning demotions above, which are kept so the patch still
applies cleanly if the flag is ever dropped.

Tested on Debian 13 (trixie) / gcc 14.2.0 / glibc 2.41 and on
Arch Linux / gcc 16.2.1 / glibc 2.42.

--- a/build.sh
+++ b/build.sh
@@ -37,10 +37,10 @@ patch -N -r - lcc/src/expr.c movfuscator/expr.patch
 patch -N -r - lcc/etc/lcc.c movfuscator/lcc.patch

 # Build the compiler driver
-make -C lcc HOSTFILE=../movfuscator/host.c CFLAGS='-g -DLCCDIR=\"$(BUILDDIR)/\"' lcc
+make -C lcc HOSTFILE=../movfuscator/host.c CFLAGS='-g -std=gnu89 -Wno-error=implicit-int -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=int-conversion -DLCCDIR=\"$(BUILDDIR)/\"' lcc

 # Build lcc with the M/o/Vfuscator backend
-make -C lcc all
+make -C lcc CFLAGS='-g -std=gnu89 -Wno-error=implicit-int -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=int-conversion' all

 # Create movcc
 ln -sfn "$BUILDDIR/lcc" "$BUILDDIR/movcc"
